From eaba885d1319ceb5cec59b6c0781f836b526270d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:06:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 360/638] [AROS] Transfer shared memory across Processes

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: cross-process-shared-memory-runtime-pass
ROOT_CAUSE: AROS shared-memory handles were tracked in per-image C++ state and SharedMemorySwitch rejected launch transfer, so a real Chromium child Process could not receive browser-owned regions.
FIX_REASON: Place region metadata and backing storage in MEMF_PUBLIC, use cross-Process atomic ownership, serialize the trusted metadata pointer at launch, and keep mapping bookkeeping local to each image.
SCOPE: base/memory/platform_shared_memory_region_aros.cc; base/memory/shared_memory_switch.cc; base/memory/shared_memory_switch_unittest.cc
VALIDATION: Hosted 16 GiB run returned host=0 and guest=0; four parameterized cases spawned child PIDs 29-32 and each child mapped and compared parent marker bytes. Evidence-aros-shmem-process-20260728.
RISK: Failed launch before deserialization can leak the transferred reference; pointer input remains trusted parent launch data until a token registry and policy boundary are added.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: direct CreateNewProc proven -> launch switch stub identified -> process-local registry removed -> MEMF_PUBLIC atomic metadata -> four-child hosted marker-byte PASS.
Evidence:-aros-shmem-process-20260728
